# Build context exclusions for `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile.
#
# This is a deny-list, not an allow-list, so a new source file is picked up
# automatically and a forgotten entry can never break the build -- only make
# the image bigger. The trade-off is that a NEW kind of secret has to be added
# here explicitly, which is why the credential patterns below are written
# broadly (.env*, *key*.json, *secret*) rather than naming today's two files.
#
# .gitignore does NOT apply to a Docker build. Both .env and gcp-key.json are
# correctly git-ignored yet sat in the build context, so `COPY . .` baked the
# real SECRET_KEY, database password, Google OAuth client secret, Mailjet
# password and the GCP service-account key into an image layer -- where they
# survive even if a later layer deletes them, and travel to anyone who pulls
# the image. Runtime config comes from the environment (docker-compose
# env_file, or the platform's secret store), never from a file in the image.
#
# NOTE ON `**/`: .dockerignore matches with Go's filepath.Match, where a bare
# `*` does NOT cross a `/`. So `__pycache__/` matches ONLY the one at the
# context root and misses app/__pycache__, app/erp/__pycache__ and the rest.
# Anything that can appear at any depth is therefore written `**/name`.

# ── Credentials — the reason this file exists ────────────────────────
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
!**/.env.example
!**/production.env.example
**/gcp-key.json
**/*key*.json
!**/package-lock.json
**/*credential*
**/*secret*
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/.gemini

# ── Bulk: ~306 MB the image has no use for ───────────────────────────
# venv/ is a stale interpreter (retired to venv.obsolete after it caused the
# WeasyPrint outage described in requirements.txt); the image installs into
# its own site-packages from requirements.txt. node_modules is Jest tooling
# for the frontend tests, which do not run in the image.
**/venv
**/venv*
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache

# ── Runtime output — must come from the container, not the build host ─
**/logs
**/*.log

# static/uploads is deliberately NOT excluded: its files are git-tracked repo
# content (item images, per migration 024_items_image), so dropping them would
# 404 every existing item photo while saving nothing. Note that uploads WRITTEN
# by a running container are still ephemeral -- that needs a mounted volume,
# which is a separate deployment decision, not a build-context one.

# ── Test, lint and docs: not used at runtime ─────────────────────────
tests
static/erp/tests
**/.coverage
coverage
htmlcov
package.json
eslint.config.js
.stylelintrc.json
requirements-dev.txt
docs
**/*.md
!README.md
audit_report.json
test_oauth.ps1

# ── Local dev scratch ────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/.vscode
.git
.gitignore
docker-compose.yml
